  "title": "Mainz Psalter",
  "summary": "Printed in Mainz by Johann Fust and Peter Schoeffer and dated 14 August 1457, the Psalter was the second major book printed in Europe. It was the first to name its printers and the date, and the first to include colour printing, with ornamental initials in red and blue. Ten copies survive, all on vellum.",
